VAA1 BBox/ROI Navigation Bug Fix Report
Date: 2026-04-24
Project: VAA1 on Python 1.0 / The-project

1. Scope

This report documents the repeated failures, regression patterns, and fix attempts related to
the VAA1 bounding box (BBox) and ROI box timing, extension, visibility, and panel propagation
workflow during the current four-day sprint.

The focus is the analyst-facing workflow where a manual correction to a BBox or ROI box must
become authoritative across the entire application.


2. Required Design Principle

The required VAA1 rule is:

- if an analyst manually corrects a BBox or ROI box
- that correction is saved
- that saved correction stands
- that saved correction becomes authoritative everywhere
- all associated panels must reflect it
- raw detections and grouped track spans may remain for traceback and fallback processing
- raw detections and grouped spans must not override the saved manual correction

In short:

MANUAL CORRECTION WINS EVERYWHERE


3. Observed Failures

The following failures were observed repeatedly:

- Extend in throws playback to wrong timestamps, including 0:00.000 and 1:05.000
- Extend in widens state without yielding usable slider navigation
- Extend out sometimes widens state without yielding usable future work area
- BBoxes surface before their corrected mark-in time
- BBoxes remain visible outside their corrected timespan
- Video panel BBoxes and leaf panel timestamps can disagree
- Saved manual timing can be ignored by the overlay rendering path
- Object-linked manual corrections can be re-overridden by grouped/raw track spans
- Selected overlays can inherit stale draft state from prior edits
- The Tools panel disappeared once due to a frontend crash
- Manual tests intended for this sprint have not been completed successfully


4. User Impact

The impact of the failures has been high:

- analyst trust in the timing system has been damaged
- manual validation has been blocked
- multiple days were consumed on the same feature family
- the workflow became harder and less predictable after several supposed fixes
- the application behaved as if it had multiple competing clocks


5. Count Of Fix Attempts

From the visible history in the latest day of the sprint alone:

- 19 distinct fix attempts were made on this same problem family

Across the full four-day sprint:

- the true number is likely much higher
- the exact total has not yet been reconstructed from all prior session history

The important conclusion is not the exact number, but that the process has retried the same
issue far too many times without stabilizing the architecture.


6. The 19 Logged Attempts From The Latest Day

1. Clicking a BBox should open at the visible frame time, not always at indication start.
2. Added geometry_keyframes for timestamped BBox geometry.
3. Improved editor placement and close behavior.
4. Tightened manual BBox visibility to the actual mark-in.
5. Tightened object override visibility to the manual mark-in.
6. Removed raw object pre-roll windows.
7. Tried making Extend in jump to an earlier opened bound.
8. Attached manual annotation timing to object overlays.
9. Made Objects leaf send explicit start/end/category/note into the video editor.
10. Refreshed Identification edit draft from the incoming annotation.
11. Unified panel navigation through shared video helpers.
12. Changed Extend in/out to widen range without moving video.
13. Added selected-manual workspace visibility.
14. Made scrub extend outside saved bounds without overdraft gating.
15. Replaced hidden padding logic with direct draft interval edits.
16. Added selectedWorkspaceAnnotationId.
17. Refreshed edit state from authoritative overlay on reopen.
18. Changed manual object overrides from one-per-track to time-aware arrays.
19. Made Objects leaf drafts derive from authoritative manual overrides.


7. Additional Regression Observed And Fixed

An additional frontend regression surfaced:

- ToolsPanel.tsx had a real crash caused by using openVideoAtTime before its declaration
- this could blank the whole Tools panel
- the fix was to use the shared video navigation helper instead

This issue was real, but separate from the main BBox authority problem.


8. Root Cause

This is not one bug. It is a failed authority model.

Too many competing time sources have been allowed to coexist:

1. raw detection timestamp
2. grouped track span
3. saved manual annotation time
4. selected editor draft time
5. slider scrub state
6. jumpToTime side effects inside extension behavior

Because these time sources compete, a correction saved in one part of the program can still be
contradicted later by another path during render or navigation.


9. Wrong Coupling Identified

The system has repeatedly shown wrong coupling between:

- overlay key and saved annotation id
- raw track span and corrected manual interval
- track-wide override and time-scoped manual correction

This wrong coupling is the main reason a saved manual correction can appear to "not take effect"
or can be re-overridden later by unrelated raw timing.


10. Where Wrong Time Enters The Program

Main leak points identified in the current frontend:

A. src/frontend/lib/video-service.ts

- groupDetectedObjectsForDisplay(...)
- builds grouped object spans using startTimestamp and endTimestamp

B. src/frontend/app/V2components/components/panels/VideoPanel.tsx

- buildLocalObjectOverlays(...)
- alignActiveObjectLabelsWithGroupedTracks(...)
- getOverlayTimeBounds(...)
- selectOverlayForEditing(...)
- scrubSelectedOverlayTo(...)
- Extend in/out button path

C. src/frontend/app/V2components/components/panels/OBJDetectionPanel.tsx

- object draft creation from grouped object rows

The practical meaning is:

- even when panel fields are manually corrected
- the visible BBox can still be rebuilt from raw/grouped timing
- especially when an object overlay is carrying a manual label/identity


11. Process Failures

The fixing process also failed in several ways:

- symptom patching happened before the architecture was frozen
- incompatible extension models were mixed together
- static and governance tests were treated as stronger proof than they really are
- fixes were reported before the exact analyst path was proven manually
- old timing logic was layered together with new timing logic instead of being removed


12. Mixed Extension Models That Caused Regressions

Three incompatible models were mixed in the same tool family:

1. hidden extension workspace / timeline padding
2. direct draft interval editing using start and end
3. jump-based extension behavior

These models conflict with one another. Their coexistence explains why the feature could appear
to improve briefly, then fail again in a different way.


13. What Has Improved

Not every change should be discarded. The following improvements remain useful:

- stricter visibility gates for manual BBoxes at actual timestamps
- timestamp-scoped geometry drafts and geometry_keyframes
- time-aware manual object overrides in the video panel
- object leaf drafts preferring manual override timing
- shared navigation helpers across panels
- Tools panel crash fix


14. What Is Still Structurally Wrong

The current BBox extension path still contains too much machinery:

- selectedOverlayTimelinePadding
- selectedOverlayOverdrafts
- selectedOverlayScrub
- selectedWorkspaceAnnotationId
- direct draft start/end
- jumpToTime calls inside extend controls

That is too much state and too many control systems for one interaction.


15. Correct Authority Chain

For corrected evidence, the correct authority chain must be:

1. saved ManualVisualAnnotation
2. all associated leaf panels read from that saved annotation
3. video BBox timing reads from that saved annotation
4. video BBox geometry reads from that saved annotation and its saved geometry keyframes
5. raw/grouped detections remain available only for fallback use and traceback use
6. raw/grouped detections must not override the saved correction


16. Required Analyst-Facing Behavior

The intended behavior from the analyst perspective is:

- mark-in and mark-out are solid anchors
- a BBox/ROI box appears only at its true saved time and location
- Extend in makes more earlier time available for editing
- Extend out makes more later time available for editing
- slider navigation operates inside the actual current draft interval
- saving commits the edited interval and geometry
- reopening the same evidence item restores the saved correction
- every associated panel shows the same corrected interval and label


17. Recommended Remediation Strategy

The next fixing phase should be strict and narrow:

1. freeze blind BBox patches
2. write one hard engineering rule:
   saved manual correction is authoritative everywhere
3. list allowed timing sources
4. list forbidden timing sources for corrected evidence
5. remove hidden extension padding from the active BBox extension path
6. remove jumpToTime side effects from Extend in/out
7. make slider min and max derive only from the current draft start/end
8. ensure corrected object and identification overlays render only from saved manual timing
9. validate one analyst path only before touching anything else:
   Identification -> Felix Leiter -> Extend in -> slider widens -> scrub works


18. Immediate Action Recommendation

The project should not treat this as a minor bug anymore. It should be handled like a focused
interaction incident:

- define the authority rule in code comments and design notes
- remove non-authoritative time paths from corrected evidence
- verify one manual test case at a time
- do not push the feature until at least one end-to-end manual navigation path passes cleanly


19. Bottom Line

The BBox/ROI navigation tool has been unstable because the program has been allowed to have
multiple competing truths about time.

The correct VAA1 rule is simpler:

MANUAL CORRECTION WINS EVERYWHERE

Until the implementation fully obeys that rule, the analyst experience will continue to suffer
from timing conflicts, extension failures, and apparent contradictions between panels.

